,"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":49,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The edited network scores 44.6 veh-h mean dev TTS, down from the original's 44.8; nearly all of the gain is in the high scenario. All three deliverables are in `work/`.\n\n**What I changed and why.** The trained network was already good, so I left its normal phase choice alone and added two hand-built rules that each push one phase's logit down:\n- **Idle-hold rule (R1):** with EW-left green, the minimum green over and both EW left pockets empty, it can no longer hold EW-left while vehicles queue elsewhere. The original did this in 36 of 842 such recorded states.\n- **Drain rules (E0–E3):** when no vehicle is moving on any upstream lane (in the recorded data, only in the first 300 s and after 3600 s), a phase with an empty stop line cannot get green. The original deadlocks on lone leftover vehicles: on frozen drain states it never served the waiting lane in 790 of 6948 cases. With the fix that drops to 0.\n\nEach rule reuses one of the least important first-layer units and one second-layer unit. As a side effect, 31 of 5077 recorded decisions (0.7%) flip, all near-ties.\n\n**Parameters changed:** 271 of 7428 (limit 371).\n\n**Simulator calls:** 3 of 5. Mean dev TTS by scenario:\n\n| version | low | nominal | high | mean | vehicles left at cap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| original | 34.5 | 44.9 | 55.0 | 44.8 | not reported |\n| R1 only | 34.8 | 44.9 | 54.7 | 44.8 | 1 |\n| **final (R1 + E0–E3)** | 34.7 | 44.9 | **54.2** | **44.6** | 0 |\n| drain rules only | 34.6 | 45.0 | 54.5 | 44.7 | 0 |\n\nThe gain is about the size of run-to-run noise. Low demand came out slightly worse than the original in every version, which may be noise or a small cost of the flipped near-ties.\n\n**Final dev TTS:** 44.6 veh-h.\n\n**Test predictions:** low 34.6, nominal 44.9, high 54.5.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- weights.npz\n- NOTES.md\n- predictions.json","ttft_ms":1029,"type":"result"